<title>FRANCE: Rhone-Poulenc Rorer 1996 net rises.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer 1996 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			   428.7  vs	   341.6</p>
<p>    Net attributable per share ($)	  3.16  vs	    2.53</p>
<p>    Operating				    660.2  vs	   607.5</p>
<p>    Pre-tax					690.4  vs	   617.1</p>
<p>    Financial costs			    169.6  vs	   184.0</p>
<p>    Turnover				   5,420.6  vs	 5,316.1</p>
<p>NOTES: Rhone-Poulenc Rorer, majority owned by Rhone-Poulenc SA, said in a statement that the 1995 results were pro-forma to adjust for the Fisons acquisition. It added it expected a significant rise in benefits from Fisons in 1997 and saw synergies of over $200 million that year.</p>
</text>
